Q:Example of a Parameterized Constructor in Java 
Definition
A Parameterized Constructor in Java is a constructor that takes arguments (parameters) to initialize an object with specific values at the time of creation.
It allows you to pass data directly when creating an object, instead of setting values later using setter methods.


package parametrized_constructor;

class Student {
    String name;
    int age;
    
    //Parameterized Constructor
    public Student(String StudentName,int StudentAge){
        //Initialize object fields with passed parameters
        name=StudentName;
        age=StudentAge;
    }
    //Method to display Student Details
    public void StudentDetails() {
        System.out.println("Name: " + name);
        System.out.println("age: " +age);
    }
}
public class Parametrized_Constructor {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        //Creating object using the Paramiterized Constructor
        Student s1=new Student("Amit" , 20);
        Student s2=new Student("Priya" , 22);
        
        // Displaying object data
        s1.StudentDetails();
        System.out.println("----------------");
        s2.StudentDetails();
    }
    
}

OUTPUT:
Name: Amit
age: 20
----------------
Name: Priya
age: 22
